          "why": "The equation tells us the position at every time, so we can solve it backwards for time.",
          "sol": "Step 1: 32 = 12 + 4t\nStep 2: 20 = 4t\nStep 3: t = 5",
          "hint": "Subtract 12, then divide by 4.",
          "subject": "math",
          "chapter": "linear_motion",
          "topic": "Finding Time from a Position Equation",
          "conceptId": "math_linear_motion_finding_time_from_a_position_equation",
