          "type": "text",
          "options": [],
          "steps": [
            "Step 1: The height must meet the base at 90°.",
            "Step 2: A sloping side may not meet the base at 90°.",
            "Step 3: Therefore, the sloping side cannot automatically be used as the height.",
            "Step 4: The perpendicular height must be used."
          ],
          "why": "The formula A = base × height requires the perpendicular height, not simply any side length.",
          "sol": "Step 1: The height must meet the base at 90°.\nStep 2: A sloping side may not meet the base at 90°.\nStep 3: Therefore, the sloping side cannot automatically be used as the height.\nStep 4: The perpendicular height must be used.",
