          "why": "6 is less than 10.",
          "sol": "Step 1: Substitute x = 6.\nStep 2: We get 6 ≤ 10.\nStep 3: This statement is true.\nStep 4: Therefore x = 6 satisfies the inequality.",
          "hint": "Compare 6 with 10.",
          "subject": "math",
          "chapter": "linear_programming",
          "topic": "Meaning of Less Than or Equal To",
          "conceptId": "math_linear_programming_meaning_of_less_than_or_equal_to",
          "skillId": "math_linear_programming",
          "subskillId": "math_linear_programming_q1"
