          "why": "Both coordinates must be zero or positive.",
          "sol": "Step 1: x ≥ 0 means x cannot be negative.\nStep 2: y ≥ 0 means y cannot be negative.\nStep 3: Therefore both coordinates must be non-negative.\nStep 4: This is the first quadrant together with its axes.",
          "hint": "Think about the signs of x and y.",
          "subject": "math",
          "chapter": "linear_programming",
          "topic": "Identifying the Feasible Region",
          "conceptId": "math_linear_programming_identifying_the_feasible_region",
          "skillId": "math_linear_programming",
          "subskillId": "math_linear_programming_q2"
