          "why": "Fractions are multiplied by multiplying corresponding numerators and denominators.",
          "sol": "Step 1: 3 × 2 = 6.\nStep 2: 5 × 7 = 35.\nStep 3: Write the result as 6/35.",
          "hint": "Multiply straight across.",
          "subject": "math",
          "chapter": "fractions",
