          "sol": "Step 1: A single die roll gives one number.\nStep 2: It cannot give both 1 and 3.\nStep 3: Therefore the events are mutually exclusive.\nStep 4: For mutually exclusive events asking for 'or', we add.\nStep 5: P(1 or 3) = 1/6 + 1/6 = 1/3.",
          "hint": "Can 1 and 3 occur on the same roll?",
          "subject": "math",
          "chapter": "probability",
          "topic": "Choosing Addition or Multiplication",
          "conceptId": "math_probability_choosing_addition_or_multiplication",
          "skillId": "math_probability",
