          "why": "Magnitude is the size of the vector quantity.",
          "sol": "Step 1: The force is given as 25 N upward.\nStep 2: 25 N gives the size of the force.\nStep 3: Upward gives the direction.\nStep 4: Therefore the magnitude is 25 N.",
          "hint": "The direction is not needed to find magnitude.",
          "subject": "math",
          "chapter": "vectors",
          "topic": "Magnitude of a Vector",
          "conceptId": "math_vectors_magnitude_of_a_vector",
          "skillId": "math_vectors",
          "subskillId": "math_vectors_q1"
