          "why": "A negative vector has the same magnitude but points in the opposite direction.",
          "sol": "Step 1: The magnitude of ⃗a is 8 N.\nStep 2: Keep the magnitude as 8 N.\nStep 3: Reverse upward to downward.\nStep 4: Therefore -⃗a = 8 N downward.",
          "hint": "The negative sign reverses the direction.",
          "subject": "math",
