          "why": "Reversing the direction changes the vector from ⃗AB to ⃗BA.",
          "sol": "Step 1: ⃗AB means movement from A to B.\nStep 2: The opposite movement must be from B to A.\nStep 3: Therefore the opposite vector is ⃗BA.",
          "hint": "Reverse the starting and ending points.",
